      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "## Getting Started with CloudScale API\n\nTo get started with CloudScale API, you'll need to authenticate your application. This involves generating an API key, which you can obtain by signing up for a CloudScale account. Once you have your API key, you'll need to include it in the header of every request you make. For example, you can use the following code snippet to set up your initial request:\n\n```python\nimport requests\n\napi_key = 'YOUR_API_KEY'\nurl = 'https://api.cloudscale.com/v1/resource'\n\nheaders = {\n    'Authorization': f'Bearer {api_key}'\n}\n\nresponse = requests.get(url, headers=headers)\nprint(response.json())\n```\n\nRemember to replace 'YOUR_API_KEY' with your actual API key. This code sends a GET request to the CloudScale API and prints the response in JSON format. You can use this as a starting point for making authenticated requests to the CloudScale API.",
